course: dictionary
lesson: 14846
title: Rakishly: dashing and bold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Mia wore her red cap rakishly on one side and grinned at her friends.» The word tells you how she wore it. She did not wear it neatly and straight. She wore it in a bold, confident way that said, look at me.
explain: Rakishly comes from «rake», an old word for a man who lived a wild, careless life. Today it is mostly used for fun, to describe someone who looks stylish and dashing, and sometimes a little cheeky.
explain: Ask yourself what the action shows about the person. A pirate who smiles rakishly is not shy. To check your guess, swap in a word like boldly or stylishly and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Rakishly» means in a dashing, stylish and confident way, often slightly careless or cheeky.
fact: «A hat worn rakishly to one side» is a hat tipped at a jaunty angle, not sitting straight.
fact: In old books, rakishly can mean in a wild way that is not respectable.
fact: Toad in The Wind in the Willows, dressed as a motorist, might wear his cap rakishly on one side to show he thinks he looks very smart and bold.
fact: Stories often use rakishly for pirates, adventurers and show-offs.
exercise: «The pirate tipped his hat rakishly and winked at the crowd.» What does rakishly mean here? | In a sad, shy way | In a sleepy, slow way | With great care and neatness | *In a dashing, bold, confident way
exercise: Toad wears his cap rakishly on one side. What does this show about him? | He is very tired | *He thinks he looks smart and bold | He is cold and wants a warmer hat | He has lost his cap
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to rakishly in its first meaning? | sleepy | nervous | gloomy | *dashing
test: «Sam wore his scarf rakishly over one shoulder as he strolled into the party.» What does rakishly suggest about Sam? | He is sleepy | He is cold and wants to go home | *He feels bold and stylish | He is lost and confused
test: In an old story, the young man lived rakishly, staying out all night with wild friends. What does rakishly mean here? | In a helpful, kind way | In a quiet, shy way | In a neat, careful way | *In a wild, not respectable way
exam: «She tilted her hat rakishly and said, Shall we go?» What does rakishly mean? | In a kind, gentle way | In a slow, careful way | In a sad, tired way | *In a dashing, confident way
